# Free models a default `dispatch.sh opencode` task (and every clawock-patrol round) tries, in
# order. The first line is the primary; the rest are the fallback pool the runner rotates through
# (after the last one it wraps back to the first). The pool is read at dispatch time, so edits
# apply without restarting the patrol service.
#
# Every entry must be in the Zen catalog (`opencode models opencode`) and cost nothing. The runner
# allows 2 attempts per pool line, so a dead entry is two wasted attempts per failing round.
#
# 2026-10-08 order. Two things decide it, in this order:
#
# 1. What the model's rounds are worth. Patrol issues of 10-01..10-08 by the model that finished
#    the round, and what became of them after verification (fixed / closed not planned or noise):
#      space-bunny-free           147 rounds   274 / 8
#      mimo-v2.6-flash-free         8 rounds    14 / 0
#      longcat-2.5-preview-free    14 rounds    14 / 0
#      fledge-alpha-free            9 rounds     3 / 0
#      nemotron-3-ultra-free       22 rounds    12 / 38
#    nemotron-3-ultra-free is removed for that: three of four issues it filed were false, and each
#    one cost a paid agent a verification. It had been 2nd since 10-07.
# 2. How the model behaves while the free tier throttles it (HTTP 429 FreeUsageLimitError). The
#    limit is per model. Since 10-06 evening the models run dry one after another during the day
#    (10-08: longcat until 09:30, space-bunny 14:00-16:00, fledge 16:10-20:20), and from about
#    01:00 to 07:57 nothing answers at all (0 of 163 attempts in three such windows; both nights
#    ended at 23:57 UTC, which points at a daily reset). So the day's rounds are bounded by the
#    quota, not by time: a failed try costs minutes and no quota, and every model with quota left
#    gets used whatever the order. The order only has to offer the best models first.
#      * longcat-2.5-preview-free surfaces the 429 (59 of 59 failures end in about 80s): first.
#      * space-bunny-free and mimo-v2.6-flash-free retry the 429 silently, so a throttled try burns
#        the runner's 300s stall timer (85 stalls in four days). They are still next: they are the
#        two best models here and 10 minutes is cheaper than leaving their quota unused.
#      * fledge-alpha-free (1M context) finished every round of 10-07 21:08-10-08 00:55 and
#        10-08 16:10-20:20 as attempt 8 of the old order. Few findings, none false.
#      * ling-3.1-flash-free has not finished a round yet (7 tries, all ended by a 503, two of them
#        after 10 and 40 minutes of real work). Unproven, so behind everything proven.
#      * exo-free answers "Endpoint is unavailable" (16 of 16) in 90s; last line, free to return.
#   removed earlier: muse-spark-1.3-contributor-free (0 of 44, 40 stalls), ling-3.0-flash-fin-free
#   (0 of 30, all stalls), mimo-v2.5-free and union-alpha (out of the catalog).
#   left out on purpose: big-pickle (2025 stealth, 200k context) and nemotron-3.5-lightning-free
#   (small fast tier) - kcn wants good models first. opencode-go is not an option: the key in
#   ~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json has no active subscription.
#
# Before adding a model or moving one up, check what its issues became (label `patrol`, closed as
# not planned / `patrol:noise`), not only whether it answers:
#   /root/tools/agent-dispatch/probe-free-models.sh --tool <model>
opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free
opencode/space-bunny-free
opencode/mimo-v2.6-flash-free
opencode/fledge-alpha-free
opencode/ling-3.1-flash-free
opencode/exo-free
